<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Klein-Venedig</h1><p class="st-meta">1528 CE – 1546 CE · capital Coro</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived German colony in Venezuela, leased by Emperor Charles V to the Welser banking house of Augsburg to pay off his debts.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1528 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/welser-family">Welser family</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-augsburg">Augsburg</a> the right to colonise and govern the province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/venezuela">Venezuela</a> in return for loans. The Welsers took over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coro-venezuela">Coro</a>, founded the year before by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-ampies">Juan de Ampíes</a>, and sent the first German governor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambrosius-ehinger">Ambrosius Ehinger</a>, in 1529.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/welser-family">Welser</a> governors used the colony mainly as a base for expeditions into the interior in search of gold and the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-dorado">El Dorado</a>. Ehinger, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolaus-federmann">Nikolaus Federmann</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georg-hohermuth-von-speyer">Georg Hohermuth von Speyer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philipp-von-hutten">Philipp von Hutten</a> led long marches into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/andecavi">Andes</a> and llanos, often with great brutality towards indigenous peoples. Little permanent settlement or farming developed, and German miners brought to the colony achieved little. Indigenous people were enslaved and sold.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1546 the Spaniard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-carvajal">Juan de Carvajal</a> killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philipp-von-hutten">Philipp von Hutten</a> and Bartholomäus <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/welser-family">Welser</a> the younger. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-the-indies">Council of the Indies</a> withdrew the Welser lease, confirmed in 1556, and the territory reverted to the Spanish <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-venezuela">Province of Venezuela</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/klein-venedig.jpg" alt="Klein-Venedig" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: PhantomFunds · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Klein-Venedig_Locator.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1528 CE – 1546 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Coro</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ambrosius Ehinger, Nikolaus Federmann, Philipp von Hutten</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/venezuela">Venezuela</a>, <a href="/countries/colombia">Colombia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Little Venice, Welser Venezuela</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1537&amp;focus=klein-venedig" aria-label="Klein-Venedig on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2763 1753 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Klein-Venedig lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3083 2009L4910 989M3083 2009L3156 2042"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4910 989h0M3156 2042h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3083 2009h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3083 2009h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Coro. <a href="/atlas?year=1537&amp;focus=klein-venedig">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
